# Non-global UI (admin, ops, internal tools)

The main md1 app is for **all signed-in users**. Do not add UI, nav, copy, or changelog entries for features that only some people use (admins, operators, internal analytics).

## Admin & internal tools

- **Routes**: keep under `/admin/*`. Protect with `isAdminEmail` in middleware and `requireAdmin()` in server code.
- **Main app UI**: no admin links, badges, or sections visible to everyone. If an admin needs a shortcut, gate it server-side (`isAdminEmail` → pass `isAdmin` boolean) and show only inside an existing personal surface (e.g. profile menu), not in sidebar headers, editor chrome, or global nav.
- **Client bundle**: never import admin email lists into client components — pass a boolean from the server.
- **What's new / marketing copy**: only user-facing product changes. Skip internal admin dashboards, analytics, and ops tooling.

## Good pattern (admin menu in profile)

```tsx
// app/page.tsx — server
isAdmin={isAdminEmail(user.email)}

// DriveProfileButton.tsx — client
{isAdmin && ( /* Admin section with /admin/* links */ )}
```

## Bad pattern

- Admin link in sidebar header next to "Notes" for all users
- Hardcoded admin emails in `"use client"` components
- Changelog entry: "New admin analytics dashboard"

## Adding a new admin email

Edit `lib/admin.ts` (`ADMIN_EMAILS`). One list, used by middleware and server checks.
